Trayvon Martin
Regardless of Trayvon Martin's background, he had the God-given right to walk to the home he was visiting in a gated community.
There are other questions that should be asked. Since Trayvon was not caught, by George Zimmerman, committing a crime, what exactly was Trayvon getting away with (Zimmerman in his 911 call "... they always get away")? There is not enough evidence to support manslaughter, since Trayvon isn't here to tell his version of events, but there is enough evidence to support self-defense because Zimmerman told his version?
If someone gets out of his car and approaches you, how would you react? Who would you consider the aggressor? How would you feel if your loved one were gunned down just because of the way he or she looked? If he or she were targeted to be the one who finally didn't get away?
Let's be honest: If Trayvon's family had not gotten the media involved, there would be no investigation. We would have never heard about it because this case would have been closed. Yes, the local media, the black community, everyone should be outraged.
